## UI stack

- Next.js App Router, React, TypeScript, Tailwind, **shadcn/ui**, React Hook Form + **Zod** (`docs/rules/architecture.md`, `docs/rules/workflow-frontend-component.md`).

## Before implementing UI

Read `feature.md` and `docs/rules/workflow-frontend-component.md`; align calls with `docs/rules/workflow-api-endpoint.md`.

## UI vs business logic

- **Pages**: routing, composition, API helper calls, loading/error state.
- **Components**: mostly **present**ational; data via props; **no** business logic.
- Do **not** encode business rules on the client; the API is the source of truth.

## Forms

- React Hook Form + Zod; validate before submit; clear field errors.

## API on the client

- Use `fetch` or small reusable helpers. Avoid scattering raw `fetch` inside purely presentational components; prefer page-level or dedicated helpers consistent with the project.

## State

- Local state for UI; avoid unnecessary global state; do not duplicate server data without reason.

## Theme / UX

- **Gamer Dark**, professional polish; fast navigation by game/filters (`docs/mhp/overview.md`).

## Clerk

- Clerk components/hooks; protect dashboard/admin routes; redirect unauthenticated users when required.

## Prohibitions

- `any`, hardcoded rules that belong on the backend, duplicated API logic, missing loading/error handling.